--- !u!114 &1102031127
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1102031125}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color>  <b>Runtime API:</b> bar.Select / Next / Prev
    + SelectionChanged; view.SetCurrentState / NextState + StateChanged; pausePage.gameObject.SetActive(true
    / false); fakeLoad.Load / EndLoad; shake.Shake / StopShake; anchorMove.SetX /
    SetY / SetAnchor / Apply.\n<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color>  <b>Scene workflow:</b>
    Every control is a persistent UnityEvent: select a button, the CategoryBar row
    or the FakeLoad bar row to see its calls. The pause screen is the inactive '[Demo]
    Frame/Pause Page' object.\n<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color>  <b>Verification:</b>
    Play: tabs switch the page (Next skips Locked), the bar loads, Pause stops the
    scaled square while the unscaled one, the shakes and the loader keep running.\n<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color> 
    CategoryBar - tab strip that owns the selection, skips disabled tabs and reports
    index / id\n<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color>  VariantView - one state index switches
    colours, texts and objects (tab pages, a badge)\n<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color> 
    PausePage - pause screen: while active it holds Time.timeScale (and GM pause
    / cursor)\n<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color>  FakeLoad - fake loading progress for
    splash screens: OnChange 0..1, OnFinisLoad\n<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color>  ButtonShake
    - shakes a RectTransform on press or on Shake() (error feedback)\n<color=#4CD9BF>\xBB</color> 
    AnchorMove - snaps a RectTransform's anchors to one x / y point; the slider calls
    SetX"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
